{
  "reason": "The plateau at 0.7670 with the DeepFM+LR+LGBM stack is caused by the base learners being dominated by a single strong signal (LGBM ~0.755) while DeepFM (~0.74) and LR add noise rather than orthogonal information; the stacking and the CatBoost addition therefore regressed because they blend in weak learners. This is a Tier 3 paradigm issue: the NN component is over-parameterized for ~8k rows of low-cardinality nominals, so the ensemble has no genuine diversity. The fix is to replace the degenerate NN/LR base layer with a trio of well-regularized GBDTs (LGBM + XGBoost + CatBoost with distinct categorical handling) that provide real, decorrelated signal, and to make the meta-learner selection OOF-accuracy aligned. Feature engineering stays untouched since the shift is at the model/ensemble level.",
  "module": ["model_design", "training_evaluation"],
  "plan": {
    "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the DeepFM/LR base learners with three distinct GBDTs — (a) LightGBM with native categorical dtypes (existing make_lightgbm), (b) XGBoost with `enable_categorical=True` on the same categorical frame, and (c) CatBoost with raw interaction categoricals passed as `cat_features` — while keeping the DeepFM class defined but unused for stacking. WHY: the data is ~21 low-cardinality nominals; GBDT variants model the coupon×expiration×direction×distance conditional means with strong regularization and each encodes categoricals differently (LGBM histogram, XGB one-hot/partition, CatBoost ordered target stats), giving genuinely decorrelated OOF probabilities that a meta-learner can exploit, unlike a 400-parameter/eight-embedding MLP on 8k rows. HOW: add factory functions `make_xgboost(seed)` (XGBClassifier n_estimators~600, max_depth~5, learning_rate~0.03, subsample/colsample~0.8, reg_lambda~1) and `make_catboost(seed)` (CatBoostClassifier iterations~600, depth~5, l2_leaf_reg~3, cat_features=indices of c0..cK, random_seed=seed, verbose=0, thread_count=2); reuse the existing `_make_lgb_frame` categorical frame (convert to XGB numpy/category frame) so train/predict encoding stays identical. Preserve signatures `_train_lgbm`, `_predict_lgbm`, `_make_lgb_frame`, `CatFeatureEngineer`, `cat_maps`, `cat_cols`, `num_cols`; persist new models under the same `bundle.joblib` keys (add `xgb_models`, `cb_models`) and keep `label_map`/`threshold` fields.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Rewrite the OOF/stack/selection logic so the base learners are {LGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost} (3 seeds each in production refit), the meta-learner is a small LGBM classifier trained on the 3 OOF columns, and candidates are {lgb_avg, xgb_avg, cb_avg, soft_vote(mean), meta_gbdt}, selected by OOF accuracy with the existing threshold search in [0.2,0.8] step 0.01. WHY: base learners now live on different probability scales, so a non-linear meta captures per-region reliability and OOF-accuracy selection is metric-faithful (avoids picking a model that only wins on a proxy); this replaces the LR meta and the DeepFM/LR OOF columns that were dragging the stack down. HOW: keep 5-fold `StratifiedKFold(shuffle=True, random_state=42)` on training rows only, keep per-fold fitting of `CouponFeatureEngineer`/`_fit_cat_maps`/`StandardScaler` on TRAIN rows only, replace `oof_fm`/`oof_lr` with `oof_xgb`/`oof_cb`, retrain the meta with `LGBMClassifier(n_estimators~200, learning_rate~0.05, num_leaves~15)` fit inside the same folds, print each candidate's OOF accuracy, and persist `use_stack`-style selection plus the chosen candidate name in the bundle. Preserve `_tune_threshold`, `make_stratified_folds`, the argparse `train`/`predict` signature, `row_id,prediction` output with original labels via `inv_map`, and fresh-process reload semantics (predict must reload `bundle.joblib` and never refit)."
  }
}
